<!-- ============================================================ -->
<!-- Mass / inertia basis (all links recomputed 2026-09-21 from the live Fusion 360 model) -->
<!--   * printed parts and the electronics envelopes: CAD volume x 1.25 g/cm3 (PETG-CF, 100% infill) -->
<!--   * servos: 23 g each, XC330-T288-T per the ROBOTIS e-manual (was 18 g, the XL330-M288-T figure) -->
<!--   * battery: 145 g flat (user-specified for the 3x 18650 pack), i.e. an effective 1.496 g/cm3 -->
<!--     over the 96.92 cm3 CAD envelope rather than the 1.25 used elsewhere, since a lithium pack is -->
<!--     denser than printed plastic. The CAD box is now 3 cells (61.0 x 76.3 x 21.0 mm); it had been -->
<!--     a 2-cell box (41.0 mm wide) in both the mesh and the mass, so assets/battery.stl was -->
<!--     regenerated to match. -->
<!--   * screws, shims, washers and the DC15 idler dummies carry no mass, keeping this file's -->
<!--     previous convention. That omits roughly 95 g of hardware robot-wide; add it if you need it. -->
<!-- Each link's mass, COM and full inertia tensor were assembled from per-part CAD mass properties -->
<!-- (parallel axis theorem), so robot.xml and robot.urdf now carry identical values. -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
